VANGERS: One for the Road
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

1. Required libraries:

   - SDL 3.2 or newer
   - SDL_net 3.2 or newer
   - libvorbis
   - SDL3-native clunk from the `sdl3` branch
     (https://github.com/stalkerg/clunk/tree/sdl3)
   - ffmpeg 6.0 or newer
   - toml11 4.4.x
   - zlib

2. Required tools:

   - CMake 4.0 or newer
   - Ninja or make

3. Building:

   $ mkdir build
   $ cd build
   $ cmake ..
   $ make

4. Running:

   $ cd data
   $ ../build/src/vangers


Windows (MSVC) prerequisites

a. Install Visual Studio 2022 or newer with the "Desktop development with C++"
   workload (CMake and Ninja are included with the workload).
b. Install vcpkg and set VCPKG_ROOT to its directory:
   https://learn.microsoft.com/vcpkg/get_started/get-started
   Dependencies are declared in vcpkg.json (sdl3, sdl3-net, libogg, libvorbis,
   zlib, toml11) and are installed automatically during the CMake configure
   step.
c. Obtain an MSVC build of FFmpeg (6.0 or newer). Prebuilt shared packages
   with headers and import libraries are available from
   https://github.com/System233/ffmpeg-msvc-prebuilt (x64, LGPL). Extract the
   archive and pass the prefix as -DFFMPEG_ROOT=<ffmpeg-prefix>.
d. Build and install clunk with the MSVC toolchain. Use the `msvc` branch of
   https://github.com/DileSoft/clunk (based on the upstream `sdl3` branch,
   with MSVC-compatible build flags), then pass its install prefix as
   -DCLUNK_ROOT=<prefix>:

   > git clone --branch msvc https://github.com/DileSoft/clunk.git
   > cmake -S clunk -B clunk/build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release ^
       -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=%VCPKG_ROOT%\scripts\buildsystems\vcpkg.cmake
   > cmake --build clunk/build --parallel
   > cmake --install clunk/build --prefix <clunk-prefix>
e. Configure and build Vangers:

   > cmake -S . -B build-msvc -G Ninja ^
       -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=%VCPKG_ROOT%\scripts\buildsystems\vcpkg.cmake ^
       -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo ^
       -DCLUNK_ROOT=<clunk-prefix> ^
       -DFFMPEG_ROOT=<ffmpeg-prefix>
   > cmake --build build-msvc --parallel

   Note: the MSVC build currently links no executable icon. The committed
   vangers.res was produced by windres as a 32-bit COFF object, which the x64
   MSVC linker rejects (LNK1112), so MSVC builds skip the resource.


OSX prerequisites

a. Install homebrew
b. brew install sdl3 sdl3_net libvorbis libogg ffmpeg toml11
c. Build/install the `sdl3` branch of clunk
   (https://github.com/stalkerg/clunk/tree/sdl3).
d. Go to 3.


Android integration

The Android host project must provide native SDL3 and SDL3_net CMake packages,
for example through their official Prefab-enabled Android archives, and an
SDL3-native Clunk build. With `ANDROID` enabled this repository builds the
static `vangers` library and exports the standard SDL3 `SDL_main()` entry point
for the host activity's native entry point. The host build must also provide a
toml11 4.4.x CMake package. Save-game files keep their existing binary format.
User preferences migrate once from `options.dat` and `controls.dat` to
`settings.toml`; the legacy files are left unchanged.
